# Test fixtures are inputs to the suite, not engine output.
# The pinned dataset and the golden snapshot must be in the repo or the
# tests cannot run on a clone.
#
# Note the ** rather than *. A single asterisk does not cross a directory
# separator, so `!tests/fixtures/*.csv` re-includes ohlcv_clean_4h.csv but NOT
# tests/fixtures/pinned/AEROUSDT_4h.csv. That is the same silent exclusion that
# nearly shipped the original fixtures missing; ** covers the subdirectories.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv
!tests/fixtures/**/*.json
!tests/fixtures/*.csv
!tests/fixtures/*.json

# Generated audit packages. docs/build/build_audit_package.py rebuilds these
# from the repository, so storing 700KB of derived bytes per round would be
# committing the same content twice.
#
# MANIFEST.md is the exception and is kept, because it records the commit the
# bundle was built from and a SHA-256 for every file in it. That is what makes
# the package reproducible and lets a later reader establish exactly which
# artifact an auditor graded -- the same argument Item 6 makes about decisions,
# applied to the audit itself.
docs/audit_package/round*/*
!docs/audit_package/round*/MANIFEST.md
